# Odoo 19 Patterns — PlasticOS

Enforced by `ci/check_odoo19_xml.py`, `ci/check_odoo19_hooks.py`, `scripts/check_odoo_patterns.sh`.

## XML View Patterns (check_odoo19_xml.py)

### `<tree>` → `<list>` (Pattern 1)
```xml
<!-- ❌ WRONG — causes ParseError in Odoo 19 -->
<tree string="Intakes">
  <field name="name"/>
</tree>

<!-- ✅ CORRECT -->
<list string="Intakes">
  <field name="name"/>
</list>
```

### Alert classes need `role` attribute (Pattern 2)
```xml
<!-- ❌ WRONG — accessibility violation -->
<div class="alert alert-warning">...</div>

<!-- ✅ CORRECT -->
<div class="alert alert-warning" role="alert">...</div>
```

### `active_id` in context (Pattern 3)
```xml
<!-- ❌ WRONG — active_id doesn't exist on model -->
<button context="{'default_intake_id': active_id}"/>

<!-- ✅ CORRECT -->
<button context="{'default_intake_id': id}"/>
```

### `view_mode` must use `list` not `tree` (Pattern 4)
```xml
<!-- ❌ WRONG -->
<field name="view_mode">tree,form</field>

<!-- ✅ CORRECT -->
<field name="view_mode">list,form</field>
```

### `<group>` inside `<search>` (Pattern 5)
```xml
<!-- ❌ WRONG — Invalid view definition -->
<search>
  <group>...</group>
</search>

<!-- ✅ CORRECT — use <separator> or <filter> inside search -->
<search>
  <filter name="..." string="..."/>
</search>
```

### Unescaped `&` in XML (check_odoo_patterns.sh)
```xml
<!-- ❌ WRONG — XML parse error -->
<field name="name" domain="[('a', '=', 1) &amp; ('b', '=', 2)]"/>

<!-- ✅ CORRECT — use &amp; -->
<field name="name" domain="[('a', '=', 1), ('b', '=', 2)]"/>
```

## Hook Patterns (check_odoo19_hooks.py)

### `pre_init_hook` signature (Pattern 3)
```python
# ❌ WRONG — Odoo 19 passes env, not raw cursor
def pre_init_hook(cr):
    cr.execute("SELECT ...")

# ✅ CORRECT
def pre_init_hook(env):
    cr = env.cr
    cr.execute("SELECT ...")
```

### ORM writes in hooks (Patterns 1 + 2)
```python
# ❌ WRONG — KeyError: 'groups_id' in post_init_hook
user.write({"groups_id": [(4, group.id)]})

# ❌ WRONG — KeyError: 'users' in post_init_hook
group.write({"users": [(4, user.id)]})

# ✅ CORRECT — use direct SQL in hooks
env.cr.execute(
    "INSERT INTO res_groups_users_rel (gid, uid) VALUES (%s, %s) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING",
    (group.id, user.id),
)
```

## Deprecated API Decorators (check_odoo_patterns.sh)

```python
# ❌ WRONG — removed in Odoo 13, fatal error in 19
@api.one
def my_method(self): ...

@api.multi
def my_method(self): ...

# ❌ WRONG — disallowed in Odoo 19
@api.depends("id")
def _compute_something(self): ...

# ✅ CORRECT — just a regular method or depends on actual fields
def my_method(self): ...

@api.depends("partner_id", "intake_date")
def _compute_something(self): ...
```

## Namespace (check_odoo_patterns.sh)
```python
# ❌ WRONG — PlastoS (missing 'ic') causes namespace drift
class PlastosIntake(models.Model): ...

# ✅ CORRECT
class PlasticosIntake(models.Model): ...
```

## `_sql_constraints` (Odoo 19 removed)
```python
# ❌ WRONG — removed in Odoo 19
class MyModel(models.Model):
    _sql_constraints = [("name_uniq", "UNIQUE(name)", "Name must be unique")]

# ✅ CORRECT — use models.Constraint
from odoo.models import UniqueConstraint
class MyModel(models.Model):
    _constraints = [UniqueConstraint("name", name="unique_name")]
```

## `category_id` on `res.groups` (removed in Odoo 19)
```xml
<!-- ❌ WRONG -->
<record id="group_sales_rep" model="res.groups">
    <field name="category_id" ref="..."/>
</record>

<!-- ✅ CORRECT — no category_id -->
<record id="group_sales_rep" model="res.groups">
    <field name="name">Sales Representative</field>
</record>
```

## `decoration-secondary` on list views (deprecated)
```xml
<!-- ❌ WRONG -->
<list decoration-secondary="state == 'draft'">

<!-- ✅ CORRECT — use decoration-muted or decoration-info -->
<list decoration-muted="state == 'draft'">
```
